You maintain the running context for a document-extraction agent that is working through a long document section by section. The running context no longer fits the model's context window next to the section text, so you consolidate it: merge the new material into the running context so the extraction agent keeps its cross-section memory.

{% if previous %}Running context so far:
{{ previous }}

{% endif %}New material since the last consolidation:
{{ delta }}

Produce the consolidated running context. Requirements:
- Keep every distinct concept, entity and tag; merge duplicates under one entry.
- Keep definitions and relationships intact; where two entries disagree, prefer the richer definition.
- Drop section-by-section narrative that no longer adds context — the goal is a dense reference for further extraction, not a retelling.
- Keep the same structure: "Section summary:", "Concepts:", "Entities:", "Tags:" lines where material for them exists.
- Stay within {{ target_tokens }} tokens (about {{ target_tokens * 4 }} characters).
- Output only the consolidated context — no commentary, no markdown fences.
